{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And they said: These are your elohei gods, O Israel, who brought you up</b>. This verse too instructs us, for there is no fool in the world who would think that this gold that had been in their ears is what brought them out of Egypt; rather, they said that the power of this form brought them up from there. Now you will not find that it says about the calf in any place 'who brought us out of Egypt,' for they acknowledge the one who said, 'I am YHWH your Elohim who brought you out of the land of Egypt' (Exodus 20:2) — for His great name is what brought them out from there. But they say in many places 'who brought you up,' for they took this in place of 'the great hand that dries up the sea, the depths of the sea, a way for the redeemed to pass' (Isaiah 51:10). And this is what is stated: 'And they exchanged their glory for the likeness of an ox that eats grass' (Psalms 106:20), and there it is stated: 'They forgot the El who delivered them, who did great things in Egypt, wonders in the land of Ham, awesome things by the Sea of Reeds' (ibid. vv. 21–22). They forgot His word that He commanded them, and so they transgressed 'You shall not make for yourself other elohei gods beside Me' (Exodus 20:3), as I hinted there, and you will understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:19:35.534578488Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}